        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Toronto Maple Leafs aren't dwelling on their 78-point finish - 8th in the Atlantic, season over - they're building for the future with aggressive, forward-looking moves. <strong>First-overall draft pick Gavin McKenna has signed his three-year entry-level contract</strong>, locking in the franchise's top prospect at a $1.075M cap hit. Backing that youth push, the club <strong>secured defenseman Emil Andrae on a two-year, $1.55M deal</strong>, a steal after acquiring him from Philadelphia in a Joseph Woll trade. Ryan Tverberg's $850K extension adds depth, while the roster now sits just $2.75M over the cap - tight, but with wiggle room. The real story? John Chica's front office is betting on a two-year window, prioritizing upside over inert stars. What to watch: <strong>how quickly McKenna and Andrae integrate into camp and whether the Leafs can shed salary to stay competitive</strong>.",
