      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Toronto Blue Jays' season is a tale of two starkly different realities, swinging from brilliance to disaster in a single day. <strong>Dylan Cease spun seven scoreless innings to blank the Mariners 2-0 in the series opener</strong>, setting a franchise record with 137 strikeouts through his first 16 starts. Yet, the very next night, the bullpen imploded as the team got just one hit and fell 11-0 to the same Mariners, a humiliation underscored by Randy Arozarena's grand slam. Now sitting at 42-47 and 11.5 games behind in third place of the AL East, the Jays are one game under.500 and on a one-game losing streak. Vladimir Guerrero Jr. turned down an All-Star invite, while Cease and Varland head to the game. <strong>The finale looms tonight at 5:00 PM ET against the Mariners, where Trey Yesavage must deliver a series win to stop the slide</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated July 5, 2026"
