      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The Toronto Raptors have finally stopped looking backward and started building forward, closing the door on a 46-36 season that ended in the Atlantic Division with a quiet third-place finish. The franchise is now all about the new blood: <strong>second-round pick Jaden Bradley has signed a two-way deal</strong>, joining Allen Graves, the first-round selection from Santa Clara, in the team's refreshed roster. Bradley, the 50th overall pick from Arizona, brings grit and floor sense to a backcourt that's hungry for identity. With Garrett Temple, the veteran guard who spent 16 years in the NBA, now heading to the Mavericks as a coach, the Raptors are shedding experience to inject youth and flexibility. The offseason is reshaping everything - cap space, camp battles, and the long-term vision. <strong>What to watch: how Bradley and Graves evolve in Summer League and whether the front office adds a veteran guard to balance the rookie surge.</strong>",
