      "title": "Leafs, Jays, Raptors, Commanders Update",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The Leafs are investing heavily in the future, with rookie Gavin McKenna set to wear No. 92 next season and a strong Day 1 free agency showing heavy dedication to the next two years. The Jays beat the Mariners 2-0 last night and face them again today at 5:00 PM ET on Sportsnet, sitting at 42-47 in third place of the AL East. Guerrero Jr. declined an All-Star invite while Cease and Varland are heading to the game, and the team is moving forward with active roster development. The Raptors signed second-round pick Jaden Bradley to a two-way deal and are building around prospects like Jamarion Sharp as they prepare for camp. The Commanders are in training camp with their next game against the Eagles on Sunday, September 13, in 70 days, and are looking ahead to Week 6 in San Francisco against the 49ers. All four teams are focused on forward momentum rather than past records."
